# Keeps secrets and unrelated files out of the build context.
#
# `.env` holds AGENT_TOKEN and the Backblaze keys. It was never copied into the
# image — the Dockerfile copies `*.mjs` and nothing else — but the whole
# directory is still sent to the Docker daemon, and a token does not belong in a
# context transfer at all.
.env
.env.*

# The Laya service builds from its own context (`build: ./layla`); including it
# here would send a Python directory to the agent's build for nothing.
layla/

# The Dockerfile copies `*.mjs`, which would otherwise sweep the test scripts
# into the image. They are run by CI, not by the server.
*.test.mjs

# Written by the agent's test, and cleaned up unless it is killed mid-run.
*.test-state.json

# Documentation and compose files are not part of the image.
*.md
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
